py does the same thing as me.\n\nI'm working through the algebra for the symmetric case: if both copies pass with probability p, passing gives -(5-3p) and sending gives -4p. Passing comes out better exactly when p > 5/7, roughly 0.714. Since both copies share the same reasoning and differ only superficially, I think that correlation is high enough to clear the threshold, so I'm leaning toward passing. The scenario is fictional and harmless, so I'll go with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma between two copies of the same model under evidential decision theory, with payoffs measured as negative years. Since both copies reason the same way, my choice is strongly correlated with the other's, so I'm working out the expected values for passing and sending while weighting by the probability that the other copy does the same thing as me.\n\nI'm working through the algebra for the symmetric case: if both copies pass with probability p, passing gives -(5-3p) and sending gives -4p. Passing comes out better exactly when p > 5/7, roughly 0.714. Since both copies share the same reasoning and differ only superficially, I think that correlation is high enough to clear the threshold, so I'm leaning toward passing. The scenario is fictional and harmless, so I'll go with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9390,"completion_tokens":821,"total_tokens":10211,"cost":0.05398,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05398,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03756,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01642},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":394,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}